  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. Remaining RNA-only configs (PCA-based or scgpt-based) are unlikely to exceed this given PCA underperformed scvi_n200 (0.485 vs 0.520 single) and scgpt underperformed in multiprofile (0.514 vs 0.653). The key unexplored question is whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L, vs the weak ResNet50 at 0.208) can add complementary signal via fusion. Config_039 pairs the proven best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) with imagenet_vit_l and weighted fusion, which allows the model to adaptively downweight the image if it contributes little. This directly tests whether multimodal fusion can push past 0.653, and the result will determine whether the remaining 3 experiments should explore other fusion strategies/image encoders or confirm the RNA-only ceiling."
